  "releaseNotes": "0.6.0-preview.3: Messaging.Nats gains inbound JetStream consumers. Typed: AddArhamNatsConsumers(...) with NatsSubscribersConfiguration (assembly-scan / per-type registration of IEventSubscriber<T>), a durable NatsConsumerHostedService that reads every event subject on the stream and dispatches via NatsMessageDispatcher (ack on known/terminal outcomes, nak→redeliver on subscriber failure) — the NATS peer to AddArhamKafkaConsumers. Raw: AddArhamNatsRawConsumer() + INatsRawEventHandler delivers every event as (eventTypeName, payload, subject) to one handler for data-driven routers (e.g. a manifest-driven notification engine), with its own durable name so it runs alongside the typed consumer. NatsConsumerOptions adds RawDurableName/AckWait/MaxDeliver/ReconnectDelay. See CHANGELOG.md.",
